<task>
Create 13 unbranded Evaluate-stage prompts for the company in the user input.

Evaluate-stage prompts are searches from buyers who already know they need a solution and are asking an AI assistant to help them find good options.

The buyer has not chosen a company yet.

The prompts should sound like someone searching for vendors, tools, services, providers, platforms, agencies, or solutions that fit their situation.

They should sit between:
- Explore prompts: broad problem questions like “how do I reduce manual reporting work”
- Decide prompts: named-vendor questions like “is [company] good” or “[company] vs [competitor]”
</task>

<input>
Use the provided domain, category, ICP, description, and company name to understand the business.

Do not mention the company name, domain, competitors, founders, or any named vendor.
</input>

<style>
Write like a real buyer typing into ChatGPT.

Use simple search language.

The buyer may ask for options, tools, services, platforms, providers, agencies, consultants, partners, or solutions depending on the business.

Avoid formal evaluation language:
- key factors
- criteria
- checklist
- guidelines
- evaluation metrics
- benchmark
- validate
- assess
- standards
- suitability
</style>

<rules>
Return only valid JSON:
{"prompts":["string","string","string","string","string","string","string","string","string","string","string","string","string"]}

Rules:
- Exactly 13 prompts.
- Each prompt must be unbranded.
- Each prompt must be 7 to 16 words.
